          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "The graph fully supports this signal. Here is the dashboard, assembled entirely from retrieved rows.\n\n## Checkpoint‑Inhibitor Myocarditis — Safety Signal Dashboard\n\n**Direct answer:** The graph holds a live, corroborated safety signal linking the anti‑PD‑1 checkpoint inhibitor (`DRUG-CPI`) to immune‑related myocarditis (`AE-MYOCARDITIS`). It is disproportionate (PRR 4.2 / ROR 4.6, χ²=58.3, 37 cases), mechanistically coherent (PD‑1/PDCD1 target → T‑cell immune‑checkpoint signaling pathway, with a genetic association), and supported by FAERS, literature, a clinical‑trial registry, and an FDA label warning.\n\n### ① Disproportionality (the signal)\n`AE-MYOCARDITIS` —[:HAS_STAT]→ `STAT-MYO-CPI` \"Disproportionality (PRR 4.2)\"\n- PRR = **4.2**, ROR = **4.6**, 95% CI **2.9–6.1**, χ² = **58.3**, cases = **37**\n- `AE-MYOCARDITIS` —[:SUSPECTED_IN]→ `DRUG-CPI` \"Checkpoint inhibitor (anti‑PD‑1)\" (class = PD‑1 inhibitor, RXN‑2563889)\n\n### ② Mechanism (biological plausibility)\n`DRUG-CPI` —[:TARGETS]→ `TGT-PDCD1` \"PD‑1 / PDCD1\" —[:IN_PATHWAY]→ `PW-CHECKPOINT` \"T‑cell immune checkpoint signaling\"\n- `DRUG-CPI` —[:CANDIDATE_SIGNAL]→ `PW-CHECKPOINT` (drug flagged into the same pathway)\n- Genetic corroboration: `GA-OT-PDCD1-MYOCARDITIS` \"Open Targets: PDCD1‑myocarditis association\" —[:GENETIC_EVIDENCE]→ `TGT-PDCD1`\n\n### ③ Supporting evidence\n- **Pharmacovigilance:** `STAT-MYO-CPI` —[:SUPPORTED_BY]→ `EV-FAERS` \"openFDA FAERS aggregate 2024Q1‑2026Q2\" (records = 37) and `EV-PMID` (synthetic PMID 99000001)\n- **Literature:** `LIT-PMID-27959767` \"Fulminant myocarditis with combination checkpoint blockade\"; `LIT-PMID-29442540` \"Management of immune‑related adverse events\" (both `-[:MENTIONS]→` the drug/AE/target)\n- **Clinical trial:** `CT-NCT02743819` \"Checkpoint inhibitor safety registry\" —[:STUDIES]→ drug/AE\n- **Regulatory:** `REG-FDA-CPI-MYOCARDITIS` \"FDA label – checkpoint inhibitor immune‑mediated myocarditis warning (BLA 125514)\" — Warnings and Precautions; withhold and start corticosteroids for grade 2+\n\n### Caveat surfaced by the graph\nA second node, `AE-CONFLICT` \"Myocarditis (conflicting status)\" (same ontology code OAE_0001489, `status=refuted`), exists with **no** SignalStat attached — a refuted/duplicate variant to keep distinct from the active signal.\n\n**Nodes cited:** `AE-MYOCARDITIS`, `AE-CONFLICT`, `STAT-MYO-CPI`, `DRUG-CPI`, `TGT-PDCD1`, `PW-CHECKPOINT`, `GA-OT-PDCD1-MYOCARDITIS`, `EV-FAERS`, `EV-PMID`, `LIT-PMID-27959767`, `LIT-PMID-29442540`, `CT-NCT02743819`, `REG-FDA-CPI-MYOCARDITIS`.",
          "toolCalls": [
