          "content": "I need to stop and be straight with you about what happened, rather than produce an answer I can't ground.\n\n## I could not query the graph — the Neo4j MCP tools failed to connect\n\nThe protocol you gave me requires that I answer **only** from the Neo4j graph, reached through the read-only MCP tools, starting with `get_neo4j_schema`. I attempted exactly that first. The result:\n\n- The `neo4j` MCP server reported **\"Still connecting\"** twice, then **\"Failed to connect: neo4j\"**.\n- Consequently `get_neo4j_schema`, `read_neo4j_cypher`, and the other read-only graph tools are **not available** in this session — I have no live channel to the graph.\n- My attempts to fall back to the BFF's own graph/diag endpoints (`curl http://localhost:8787/api/diag`) are gated behind a permission prompt that hasn't been granted, so I can't confirm graph reachability that way either.\n\nBecause **zero rows were retrieved**, I have nothing to ground a statement on. The seed node ids you supplied (`REG-FDA-CPI-MYOCARDITIS`, `CT-NCT02743819`, `EV-PMID`, `LIT-PMID-27959767`, `PW-CHECKPOINT`) are explicitly *not* evidence, and I won't cite them or reconstruct a dashboard from prior knowledge — that would violate the \"only from the graph\" rule and produce a fabricated safety signal, which is exactly the wrong thing to do in a pharmacovigilance context.\n\n## What I need to proceed\n\nThis matches the known failure mode in this repo's `CLAUDE.md` (MCP/CLI tools live in `~/.local/bin`; a process launched without that on PATH can't spawn `uvx`/the MCP server). To get me a working graph channel, one of:\n\n1. **Restart the MCP-backed BFF** from a shell that has `~/.local/bin` on PATH, then re-run this session so the `neo4j` MCP server registers — or\n2. **Approve the diagnostic curl** so I can check `/api/diag` (`checks.uvx`, `checks.claudeBin`) and confirm whether it's the PATH issue, or\n3. Tell me it's fine to reach the graph through the **BFF's read-only query endpoint** and grant that one Bash/curl permission — I'll still do schema-first, minimal read-only Cypher.\n\nOnce I have a live read-only path, I'll run the schema call, then targeted Cypher to assemble the three dashboard panels you asked for — **disproportionality** (the reporting/ROR signal), **mechanism** (the pathway to myocarditis), and **supporting evidence** (regulatory action, trial, literature) — each grounded in returned rows with node ids/labels cited.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?",
